# Laboratory Manual, Electrical Engineering 25.

**Authors:** 

## Abstract
Developed as part of a series of materials in the electrical engineering sequence developed under contract with the United States Office of Education, this laboratory manual provides nine laboratory projects suitable for a second course in electrical engineering. Dealing with resonant circuits, electrostatic fields, magnetic devices, and electronic devices, it involves the following projects: (1) electrostatic field plotting, (2) amplifier frequency response, (3) oscillator circuits, and (4) analog computer applications. There are also projects on the characteristics (l) triodes, (2) inductors, (3) transformers, and (4) transistors. (DH)

